      "writtenOn": "2026-08-19T04:20:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a real problem found during testing. When D-Bus returns empty strings for properties (which occurs during early boot phases or with certain hardware configurations), bmcweb currently includes them in the Redfish response with empty values like:\n\n\"PartNumber\": \"\"\n\"SerialNumber\": \"\"\n\nThe Redfish Service Validator flags these as schema violations since these properties should either contain valid values or be omitted entirely per the Redfish specification.\n\nThis patch ensures properties are omitted when D-Bus returns empty values, which makes the response compliant with the Redfish schema.",
      "parentUuid": "d6026488_1524a4f4",
      "revId": "62f7280495469332049ec9343deadf222e38c2ee",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
